{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00294",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.64,
      "end_seconds": 3.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. Can I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.99,
      "end_seconds": 9.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.59,
      "end_seconds": 16.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "It's occasional chest tightness, mostly. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.1,
      "end_seconds": 18.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.16,
      "end_seconds": 30.92,
      "duration_seconds": 11.76,
      "text": "For about three months, I'd say. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.55,
      "end_seconds": 37.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.04,
      "end_seconds": 53.94,
      "duration_seconds": 14.9,
      "text": "I get some relief from resting. I notice it more with walking uphill. Pretty moderate, if I'm being honest. It happens a few times a day. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.51,
      "end_seconds": 57.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Right, does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.49,
      "end_seconds": 63.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Ankle swelling in the evenings goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.35,
      "end_seconds": 77.78,
      "duration_seconds": 13.43,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.59,
      "end_seconds": 80.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.83,
      "end_seconds": 85.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Have you had any coughing up blood, bruising or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.31,
      "end_seconds": 90.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "I haven't had coughing up blood, bruising or black stools, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.49,
      "end_seconds": 99.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.62,
      "end_seconds": 102.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "No, I've never had anything serious."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.57,
      "end_seconds": 109.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.03,
      "end_seconds": 110.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.28,
      "end_seconds": 114.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.3,
      "end_seconds": 118.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Well, yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.48,
      "end_seconds": 119.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.51,
      "end_seconds": 121.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Nothing, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.36,
      "end_seconds": 125.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.46,
      "end_seconds": 134.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.92,
      "end_seconds": 161.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 64, pressure 125 over 71, respiratory rate 15. And temp 36.6 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.88,
      "end_seconds": 164.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.61,
      "end_seconds": 170.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.71,
      "end_seconds": 176.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.82,
      "end_seconds": 181.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.32,
      "end_seconds": 197.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Chest is clear and heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.84,
      "end_seconds": 203.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.02,
      "end_seconds": 221.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "The scar on your chest has healed well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.85,
      "end_seconds": 237.81,
      "duration_seconds": 13.96,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like stable recovery after the heart event. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.69,
      "end_seconds": 240.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.12,
      "end_seconds": 260.4,
      "duration_seconds": 18.28,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with stable recovery after the heart event do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had occasional chest tightness for about three months, moderate, and no coughing up blood or bruising."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.8,
      "end_seconds": 263.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.2,
      "end_seconds": 267.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.01,
      "end_seconds": 268.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.95,
      "end_seconds": 306.8,
      "duration_seconds": 23.85,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Let's get a lipid profile, for cardiovascular risk. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's use atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night, long term. That should help with cardiovascular risk. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Please don't stop the blood thinner on your own, even if you feel fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.33,
      "end_seconds": 330.69,
      "duration_seconds": 23.36,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Cardiac rehab is worth doing, it really helps your confidence. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. I'd like to see you again in three months. Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.02,
      "end_seconds": 338.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "So, I take the atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night and come back in three months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.72,
      "end_seconds": 343.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.68,
      "end_seconds": 348.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.24,
      "end_seconds": 350.18,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}